    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44711" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπᾰτέρεια</span></b> , ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατήρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>daughter of a noble sire</i>, epith. of Helen, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.292
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.227
			</span></i>; of Tyro, <i><span class="en">
				11.235
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑταῖραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					2.29
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.570
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.688
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of places,
				<i>belonging to a noble father</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					68
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
